<title>JAPAN: Japan June corn imports rise 11.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June corn imports rise 11.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in June totalled 1,372,111 tonnes, up 11.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			   June 97	 May 97	 June 96</p>
<p> Total		1,372,111     1,355,417     1,230,556</p>
<p> Feed corn total    864,715	 886,069	 735,327</p>
<p> Others		 507,396	 489,348	 495,229</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   819,397	 832,389	 735,327</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports during the first six months of calendar 1997 reached 5,057,240 tonnes, against 7,908,159 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3 3432-7391)</p>
</text>
